  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "encouragement, urging on",
      "explanation": "Strong encouragement or rallying of someone to keep going or try harder. Stronger and more forceful than simple 応援."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "15022_gekirei_ex1",
      "japanese": "{選手|せんしゅ}を{激励|げきれい}した。",
      "english": "I encouraged the athletes.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "15022_gekirei_ex2",
      "japanese": "{監督|かんとく}の{激励|げきれい}でチームが{奮起|ふんき}した。",
      "english": "The team was fired up by the coach's encouragement.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "15022_gekirei_ex3",
      "japanese": "{社長|しゃちょう}が{現場|げんば}を{訪|おとず}れ、{社員|しゃいん}たちを{激励|げきれい}して{回|まわ}った。",
      "english": "The company president visited the work sites and went around encouraging the employees.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE: {激励|げきれい} implies a more forceful, spirited form of encouragement than {応援|おうえん} or {励|はげ}まし. It often comes from a superior or leader to those under them.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {激励|げきれい}の{言葉|ことば}: words of encouragement\n- {激励|げきれい}する: to encourage, to rally\n- {激励|げきれい}を{受|う}ける: to receive encouragement\n- {激励|げきれい}{会|かい}: pep rally, encouragement gathering",
